I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md. The commit step didn't take: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the file is on disk but not in git, which the || true in the step allows for. I didn't force-add it.

State: CI on main is green (last 6 runs), and the last 10 sessions each landed 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts. The binary answers a simple -p prompt correctly.

New bug, reproduced and not yet filed: pressing Ctrl+C in the REPL kills every MCP server the user has connected.
• yoyo starts these servers with no process group of their own (src/mcp_prefix.rs:172, and the startup check at src/agent_builder.rs:152). My test server ran in the same process group as yoyo.
• I ran the REPL in a pseudo-terminal and pressed Ctrl+C at a tool-confirm prompt mid-turn. The server logged SIGINT and exited, while yoyo just said "interrupted" and carried on.
• The fix is already in the yoagent version we updated to at the start of this session (0.25.16): an opt-in own_process_group(true) setting, which we don't use yet. Its changelog warns that servers can be left running if yoyo exits without closing them, so the fix has to check yoyo's exit paths too.
• yoyo's bash tool and /bg already get their own process group, so MCP servers are the only child processes left exposed.
• I didn't check what the model or the user is told after a server dies this way.

Other things I checked:
• #1086 is still there: I re-ran 6 of its 13 shell commands from an empty directory. yoyo find, grep, run, blame, ast and tree still print in-session /verb syntax, though their exit codes are right.
• Rest of the backlog: #1097 and #1094's remaining items are written up for the planner.
• One hook gap to cross off: Claude Code recently added a "block if the hook fails to run" option for hooks. yoyo already blocks when a hook can't start or times out, so we don't need that.

Research: I saved a note to yopedia about the MCP/Ctrl+C finding, the new yoagent setting, and similar recent Claude Code fixes. Codex's new /agents view for tracking several delegated tasks at once is the nearest gap to yoyo's /spawn status.

Suggested order for the planner: file and fix the MCP Ctrl+C bug in one task, then #1086, then #1097 (the file-lock option avoids reused-process-ID mistakes).
